// Strength Reduction (Address Calculation)
// C: array[i*8 + 4]
// Uses LEA (Load Effective Address) to combine
// multiplication (shifting) and addition quickly.
// Equivalent to RAX = RCX*8 + 4
; LEA RAX, [RCX*8 + 4]

// Zeroing Register Optimization
// Prefer XOR over MOV 0 for performance and size
// Breaks data dependency chains on previous content
; XOR EAX, EAX
; // EAX = 0

// Loop Unrolling and Vectorization (SIMD/SSE)
// C: for (i=0..N) a[i] += b[i]; (Floats)
// Processes 4 elements simultaneously
; MOVUPS XMM0, [RDI]   // Load 4 floats (16 bytes)
; ADDPS XMM0, [RSI]    // Add 4 floats
; MOVUPS [RDI], XMM0   // Store result

// Move Elimination/Constant Propagation
// C: int a = 10; int b = 10; return a + b;
; MOV EAX, 20          // Result computed at compile time

